This is an LPC driver test/demo environment.

Commands you can actually run here:
  look [id]      look at the room, or at something here
  examine [id]   same as look
  take <id>      pick up something in the room
  get <id>       same as take
  drop <id>      put down something you are carrying
  inventory      list what you are carrying
  inv            same as inventory
  say <text>     speak to everyone in your room
  who            list connected players
  eval <code>    compile and run one LPC statement, e.g.
                 eval return 1 + 1;
  help           show this list again
  quit           save and disconnect
  shutdown       stop the whole driver process

Movement (each room's own description lists its real exits):
  north / south / east / west

Talking to people:
  talk <name>               start a conversation
  talk <name> about <topic> ask about something specific

Once you are holding the wand of creation (left on the gatehouse
worktable, and handed to you automatically when you arrive):
  clone <path>   clone a copy of an existing object into this
                 room or your pack
  purge <name>   clear away an unwanted object in the room
  create <name>  build something new
  npc <name>     create a living NPC in this room
  edit <id> <text> rewrite a created object's description
  room <name>    write a new room (domain or /data/created/)
  exit <dir> <path> link this room to another
  domain [name]  set or show the active domain (none clears)
  save           write the active domain world graph
